  "body": "### Summary\nAs a reader who set « Bouton + » to « Pas d'icône », I want legacy's « Répondre » entry in the topic's « … » menu, so that I can still write a plain reply without quoting a message.\n\nRefs #655 (inventory row 26).\n\n### Legacy (reference `87fe0d1c`)\n- Added by `196620d2` with the « Bouton + » setting. `HFRswift/Swift/MessagesView.swift` @ `87fe0d1c`: the reader's toolbar `Menu` holds « Rechercher », then « Répondre » (`square.and.pencil`, `openForumReplyComposer()`, whenever the page has an answer form, `topicAnswerURL != nil`), then the page items (`:5575-5600`); the same entry in the other toolbar variant at `:5832-5842`. It is there in every « Bouton + » mode, so « Pas d'icône » hides the floating button but keeps a reply path.\n\n### SwiftHFR today (`dev-swift` @ `e672de7c`)\n- `App/SwiftHFR/Reader/ReaderOverflowToolbar.swift:3-5`: « Répondre » is left out of the overflow on purpose, \"it is a bottom-bar button (`ReaderPageControls`)\"; that follows LOT-186 D2 (`docs/lots/LOT-186-reader-chrome.md:29`, b·operator: \"Répondre\" moved to the bottom bar).\n- `Reader/TopicReaderView.swift:236-239`: with `reply_button_behavior` = hidden there is no reply symbol, so no reply button at all; the « Bouton + » info bubble (`Settings/TopicsSettingsModel.swift:84`, #1062) says « réponds depuis le menu d'un message (« Citer ») ». So « Pas d'icône » leaves no plain (quote-less) reply.\n- GAP-102 does not mention it.\n\n### Decision needed (operator)\nD2 decided where « Répondre » lives when there is a button; it did not decide the « Pas d'icône » case. Options:\n1. Add « Répondre » to the « … » overflow when the bottom-bar button is absent (« Pas d'icône »), legacy's order (after « Rechercher »).\n2. Add it to the overflow in every mode, as legacy.\n3. Keep it as is and record the difference in GAP-102.\n\n### Acceptance criteria (options 1 or 2)\n- « Répondre » opens the same composer as the bottom-bar button (`requestReply()`), only when the page has an answer form and the user is logged in.\n- `ReaderOverflow.entries` gains the entry; its pure test pins the order; the header comment of `ReaderOverflowToolbar.swift` is updated.\n\n### Ledger (for the PR that closes this)\n`gap-edit` GAP-102 (SwiftHFR final), whichever option.",
